      "source": [
        "# **Can we predict Zone 1 demand one hour ahead, and how much better is a real model than just assuming demand repeats?**"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "08yC3r19Sz7y"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "This project predicts power comsumption in Tetouan, Morocco, one hour ahead, using 10-minute grid measurements from 2017. It compares linear regresson and random forest regressor prediction models to the baseline of assuming demand repeats. (same time yesterday)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "pdNXn1EXAuTG"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Results"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "iGlPZ6G4Xl36"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "linear regresson model had a MAE of 812.040 and an r^2 value of 0.969. The MAE is 19.4% lower than the one day baseline\n",
        "\n",
        "Random forest regressor model has a MAE of 1153.854 and a r^2 of 0.939. The MAE 14.5% higher than the one day baseline\n",
        "\n",
        "the one day baseline (one day ago) had a MAE of 1007.404 and a r^2 of 0.941\n",
        "\n",
        "the persistence (load 1 hr ago) had a MAE of 1857.006 and a r^2 of 0.826"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "N6klDhh2GwZl"
      }
    },
